    "content": {
      "component": "blog_article",
      "sharepoint_id": "44",
      "title": "Inclusivity in Motion: A Night of Salsa and Inspiration",
      "description": "",
      "date": "Oct 10, 2023",
      "read_time": "4 min read",
      "author": "Dr Asad I Mian",
      "isGlobal": true,
      "banner_image": {
        "fieldtype": "asset",
        "_local": "44-Banner.jpg"
      },
      "thumbnail": {
        "fieldtype": "asset"
      },
      "languages": [],
      "show_share": true,
      "show_similar": true,
      "similar_show_header": true,
      "category": "",
      "isFeatured": null,
      "body": [
        {
          "component": "rich_text",
          "content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In the grand tapestry of life, sometimes the most extraordinary moments occur when we least expect them. An event, initially designed to celebrate dance and music, evolved into something far more profound - a night of inclusivity and inspiration. In this "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "'human interest' ",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "story, we shine a spotlight on three remarkable individuals: Haris, Rohail, and Amna. Their stories are a testament to the power of empathy, compassion, and the unwavering spirit of inclusivity."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "It all started with their expressed eagerness to participate in Zalsa -the Latin American dance aspect of it per se. As you can see in the photo, two "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "'differently abled'",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " individuals are in wheelchairs. Haris, a resilient young man with a passion for life, has been navigating the world from his wheelchair. Despite facing physical challenges, he radiates enthusiasm and curiosity. Amna's journey is a testament to the power of the human spirit. Her diagnosis has not deterred her from pursuing her passions."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The person in the photograph above vehemently denying usage of a wheelchair is Rohail. His mother, Shumaila Khan, Manager of the Physical Therapy Department at AKUH, tells me that Rohail does not like wheelchairs and prefers being helped by his attendant. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"Rohail was born prematurely at 31 weeks gestation. Birth asphyxia (lack of oxygen for the baby's brain during the labour and delivery period) led to spastic cerebral palsy\",",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " Shumaila told me when I requested more details about Rohail. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "He has had a rollercoaster of a life already for someone who is merely seventeen. Notwithstanding, Rohail is a dynamic force of nature, and a beacon of positivity. His background is as diverse as his interests, making him a unique and vibrant presence in any room. Fondly called 'Bugs' by his friends and family, Rohail is immensely sociable. "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rohail is quite jet set: eager to travel outside of Pakistan (for cricket per se) whenever he can - Bugs' story is one of triumph over adversity, proving that labels cannot define a person's potential."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "I was grateful to Namra Nasir, the founder and CEO of Adaptive Fitness Academy (AFA), a neurorehabilitation center, for hosting the event. I have known Namra for several years now since the time she worked as our biomedical engineer mentor/advisor at the "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Critical Creative Innovative Thinking (CCIT) forum",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "/ccit/Pages/home.aspx",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " - Aga Khan University's first and to date only co-ideation | innovation | incubation hub. I think the time Namra spent with us at AKU was merely a steppingstone to entrepreneurship. Her passion and brainchild, AFA has a simple-yet-poignant mission: "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "advancing human ability through enabling accessible and inclusive fitness training for everyone.",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " This has always motivated me to support its cause. Zalsa, the combination of Zumba and Salsa, is about inclusivity through movement, enhancing humanity's capacity, and transcending real or perceived limitations. The synergy between AFA and Zalsa is amazing, and thus Namra and I continue to work together whenever we can, as happened the past weekend.  "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "That particular Zalsa evening was destined to be extraordinary. As the music filled the room and the dance floor came to life, an atmosphere of inclusivity enveloped everyone present. It became more than just a dance; it was a celebration of life, determination, and the power of unity. It was indeed a proud moment for team Zalsa to 'perform' for Haris, Amna and Rohail. What was coolest though was seeing them vibe along while Namra's ability to make wheelchairs appear kickass tech on the dance floor did not go unnoticed! "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "image",
                "attrs": {
                  "src": "/blogs/PublishingImages/zalsa1.jpg",
                  "alt": ""
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The mandatory mirror selfie after the session.",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "What unfolded that night touched the hearts of all. It was about bearing witness to extraordinary individuals who refused to let circumstances define their existence. It was about dancing with determination, paving the way for inclusivity, and shattering stereotypes with grace. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "'Handicapped'",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "'disabled'",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " are such limiting descriptors for the human ability as AFA teaches us. Inclusivity is not just a word; it's a powerful force that has the potential to transform lives. Haris, Rohail, and Amna exemplify the strength of the human spirit and the boundless possibilities that exist when empathy, compassion, and inclusivity converge. Their stories remind us that we can all be part of creating a more inclusive world where every individual's unique journey is celebrated and embraced."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "image",
                "attrs": {
                  "src": "/blogs/PublishingImages/zalsa2.jpg",
                  "alt": ""
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Graduating from high school and other fun moments - pics shared by Rohail, with love!",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Author's Note: ",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "This story is a tribute to Haris, Rohail, and Amna, and to everyone who champions inclusivity and diversity. It is a reflection of the compassion that exists within our communities and the profound impact it can have on us all. Let us celebrate abilities, not limitations."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
